msgid "What is Complexity Analysis?"
msgstr "什么是复杂度分析？"

msgid "An **algorithm** is a sequence of steps for solving a problem, *e.g.* searching for a value in an array of $n$ elements. There is usually more than one algorithm that solves the same problem. **Complexity analysis** studies how the resources an algorithm needs grow with the **input size** $n$. There are two types of complexity:"
msgstr "**算法**（algorithm）是解决一个问题的一系列步骤，*例如*在含有 $n$ 个元素的数组中查找一个值。解决同一个问题的算法通常不止一种。**复杂度分析**（complexity analysis）研究算法所需的资源如何随**输入规模** $n$ 增长。复杂度有两种："

msgid "**Time complexity**: how the number of operations an algorithm needs grows with $n$."
msgstr "**时间复杂度**：算法所需的操作次数如何随 $n$ 增长。"

msgid "**Space complexity**: how the memory an algorithm needs grows with $n$."
msgstr "**空间复杂度**：算法所需的内存如何随 $n$ 增长。"

msgid "In this chapter, we focus on time complexity. To see why it matters, let's compare two algorithms that search an array for a value."
msgstr "在本章中，我们关注时间复杂度。为了说明它为什么重要，我们来比较两种在数组中查找值的算法。"

msgid "Linear search"
msgstr "线性查找"

msgid "**Linear search** checks the elements of the array one by one from left to right, until it finds the value or reaches the end of the array."
msgstr "**线性查找**（linear search）从左到右逐个检查数组中的元素，直到找到该值或到达数组末尾。"

msgid "**Code** {{code_runner_header}}"
msgstr "**代码** {{code_runner_header}}"

msgid "**[Line 4 to 13]** `linearSearch` compares `x` with `a[0]`, `a[1]`, `a[2]`, and so on. It returns `true` as soon as it finds `x`, or `false` after it checks every element. We count the element comparisons in `comparisons`, which is passed by reference."
msgstr "**[第 4 到 13 行]** `linearSearch` 依次把 `x` 与 `a[0]`、`a[1]`、`a[2]` 等进行比较。它一旦找到 `x` 就返回 `true`，检查完所有元素仍未找到则返回 `false`。我们用按引用传递的 `comparisons` 来统计元素比较的次数。"

msgid "Searching for `11` in the array below takes 4 element comparisons:"
msgstr "在下面的数组中查找 `11` 需要 4 次元素比较："

msgid "**How many comparisons does linear search need in an array of $n$ elements?**"
msgstr "**在含有 $n$ 个元素的数组中，线性查找需要多少次比较？**"

msgid "**Best case:** the first element matches, so we need only **one** element comparison."
msgstr "**最好情况：** 第一个元素就匹配，所以只需要**一次**元素比较。"

msgid "**Worst case:** the value is the last element or is not in the array, so we need $n$ element comparisons."
msgstr "**最坏情况：** 要找的值是最后一个元素或者不在数组中，所以需要 $n$ 次元素比较。"

msgid "Binary search"
msgstr "二分查找"

msgid "If the array is **sorted** in ascending order, we can do much better. **Binary search** works as follows:"
msgstr "如果数组按升序**排好序**，我们可以做得好得多。**二分查找**（binary search）的步骤如下："

msgid "Compare the value with the **middle** element of the search range, which is initially the whole array."
msgstr "把要找的值与查找范围的**中间**元素进行比较，查找范围最初是整个数组。"

msgid "If the value equals the middle element, it is found."
msgstr "如果该值等于中间元素，就找到了。"

msgid "If the value is smaller than the middle element, it can only be in the left half, so we continue searching the left half."
msgstr "如果该值小于中间元素，它只可能在左半部分，所以继续在左半部分查找。"

msgid "If the value is larger than the middle element, it can only be in the right half, so we continue searching the right half."
msgstr "如果该值大于中间元素，它只可能在右半部分，所以继续在右半部分查找。"

msgid "For example, searching for `11` in the same sorted array takes only 3 comparisons:"
msgstr "例如，在同一个有序数组中查找 `11` 只需要 3 次比较："

msgid "**[Line 6 and 7]** The search range is from index `low` to index `high`. Initially, it is the whole array."
msgstr "**[第 6 和 7 行]** 查找范围是从下标 `low` 到下标 `high`。最初它是整个数组。"

msgid "**[Line 9]** `mid` is the index of the middle element of the search range. When the range has an even number of elements, there are two middle elements, and we pick the right one, *e.g.* index 4 for the range 0 to 7, as in the example above."
msgstr "**[第 9 行]** `mid` 是查找范围中间元素的下标。当范围内的元素个数为偶数时，有两个中间元素，我们选择靠右的那个，*例如*对于范围 0 到 7 选择下标 4，与上面的例子一致。"

msgid "**[Line 11 to 17]** If `x` equals `a[mid]`, we found it. Otherwise, we shrink the search range to its left half or its right half. In this implementation, each iteration compares `x` with one element, `a[mid]`, so we count it as one comparison."
msgstr "**[第 11 到 17 行]** 如果 `x` 等于 `a[mid]`，就找到了。否则，我们把查找范围缩小为它的左半部分或右半部分。在这个实现中，每次迭代把 `x` 与一个元素 `a[mid]` 进行比较，所以我们把它算作一次比较。"

msgid "**[Line 8]** If the search range becomes empty, *i.e.* `low > high`, `x` is not in the array."
msgstr "**[第 8 行]** 如果查找范围变为空，*即* `low > high`，说明 `x` 不在数组中。"

msgid "**How many comparisons does binary search need in an array of $n$ elements?**"
msgstr "**在含有 $n$ 个元素的数组中，二分查找需要多少次比较？**"

msgid "**Best case:** the middle element matches, so we need only **one** comparison."
msgstr "**最好情况：** 中间元素就匹配，所以只需要**一次**比较。"

msgid "**Worst case:** the search continues until there is only one element left in the search range. Each comparison **halves** the search range:"
msgstr "**最坏情况：** 查找一直持续到查找范围内只剩下一个元素。每次比较都会把查找范围**减半**："

msgid "After 1 comparison, the search range has $n/2 = n/2^1$ elements."
msgstr "比较 1 次之后，查找范围有 $n/2 = n/2^1$ 个元素。"

msgid "After 2 comparisons, the search range has $n/4 = n/2^2$ elements."
msgstr "比较 2 次之后，查找范围有 $n/4 = n/2^2$ 个元素。"

msgid "..."
msgstr ""

msgid "After $k$ comparisons, the search range has about $n/2^k$ elements."
msgstr "比较 $k$ 次之后，查找范围大约有 $n/2^k$ 个元素。"

msgid "The search range has one element left when $n/2^k \\approx 1$, *i.e.* $2^k \\approx n$, so $k \\approx \\log_2 n$. In the worst case, binary search needs approximately $\\log_2 n$ comparisons."
msgstr "当 $n/2^k \\approx 1$，*即* $2^k \\approx n$ 时，查找范围只剩下一个元素，所以 $k \\approx \\log_2 n$。在最坏情况下，二分查找大约需要 $\\log_2 n$ 次比较。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "The worst-case number of comparisons of linear search grows **linearly** with $n$, while that of binary search grows **logarithmically** with $n$. For an array of one million elements, linear search may need one million comparisons, while binary search needs only about 20, since $2^{20} \\approx 10^6$."
msgstr "线性查找在最坏情况下的比较次数随 $n$ **线性**增长，而二分查找的比较次数随 $n$ **对数**增长。对于一个有一百万个元素的数组，线性查找可能需要一百万次比较，而二分查找只需要大约 20 次，因为 $2^{20} \\approx 10^6$。"

msgid "Why not just measure the running time?"
msgstr "为什么不直接测量运行时间？"

msgid "**Why do we count operations instead of measuring the running time of a program in seconds?** The measured running time of a program depends on many things other than the algorithm:"
msgstr "**为什么我们要统计操作次数，而不是测量程序以秒为单位的运行时间？** 程序实测的运行时间除了取决于算法之外，还取决于许多其他因素："

msgid "the hardware, *e.g.* a faster or slower computer,"
msgstr "硬件，*例如*计算机的快慢，"

msgid "the compiler,"
msgstr "编译器，"

msgid "the programming language, and"
msgstr "编程语言，以及"

msgid "the input."
msgstr "输入。"

msgid "However, the choice of algorithm matters, especially for large inputs. Suppose we run linear search on a **faster** computer, and binary search on a much **slower** computer, and we measure the worst-case running time:"
msgstr "然而，算法的选择很重要，尤其是对于大规模输入。假设我们在一台**较快**的计算机上运行线性查找，在一台慢得多的计算机上运行二分查找，并测量最坏情况下的运行时间："

msgid "Input size $n$"
msgstr "输入规模 $n$"

msgid "Linear search: faster computer"
msgstr "线性查找：较快的计算机"

msgid "Binary search: slower computer"
msgstr "二分查找：较慢的计算机"

